lantern-pr 1
# 4
#title feat: read GitHub pull request state from the host
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/4
#branch feat/github-pr-host-state
#base main
#opened 2026-11-06
#head eae2007442dfee17f05f7f070f4b12c5af3dd169
#describe what The pull request view asks GitHub for the state of each pull request, the way it already did for Bitbucket, and the host answer wins over what commit messages say.
#describe what A GitHub rate limit, a bad token, a 404, a timeout or a network error give the existing note and keep the git state.
#describe before A GitHub project got no host state, so a pull request merged by squash or rebase showed as open.
#describe after The squash-merged pull request shows merged, a closed unmerged one shows declined, and an open one stays open.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint, the full test suite, compile, the skills check and a stub-API check of the strip, all green; the real api.github.com was not driven.
