#reason src/main/lantern-host-drivers.ts Puts what differs per code host in one table so the status layer stays generic.
#reason src/main/lantern-host-github.ts Reads a GitHub pull request's state and base branch and tells a rate limit from other failures.
#reason test/e2e/pr-host-state.spec.ts Shows the strip of a GitHub-origin project against a stub API, with screenshots on request.
#reason test/helpers/fake-github.ts Gives the tests a local GitHub API that answers states, errors and rate limits.
#reason test/lantern-host-github.test.ts Proves the GitHub states, failures, rate limit, account choice and token secrecy.
#reason CONTRIBUTING.md Tells contributors a new code host needs a driver as well as a provider row.
#reason docs/architecture.md Explains how the view takes a pull request's state from git and from the host.
#reason docs/getting-started.md States precisely what an account gives the view: the host's state of each pull request.
#reason docs/primitives.md Names the host state capability and its tests so the next change composes it.
#reason package.json Adds the script that runs the stub-API check of the pull request strip.
#reason src/main/lantern-host-account.ts Resolves the project's account for either code host instead of Bitbucket only.
#reason src/main/lantern-host-origin.ts Recognises GitHub's ssh.github.com remote through the provider table.
#reason src/main/lantern-host-request.ts Exposes the redirect-safe request with its status and headers for the GitHub request.
#reason src/main/lantern-host-status.ts Asks whichever host the origin names and lets its answer override git, pausing on a rate limit.
#reason src/main/lantern-prs.ts Hands the host service every record so it can choose whom to ask.
#reason src/shared/lang/en/messages.json Adds the notices for hosts that are asked about merged pull requests too.
#reason src/shared/providers.ts Lists the extra git remote hosts of a provider, GitHub's ssh.github.com.
#reason test/auth-host-detection.test.ts Pins the ssh.github.com forms and the lookalike hosts that must stay refused.
#reason test/helpers/git-repo.ts Adds a squash merge helper and a URL option to the record writer.
#reason test/helpers/host-world.ts Names the GitHub origin the new tests use.
#reason test/lantern-host-status.test.ts Keeps the non-Bitbucket skip test honest now that GitHub is asked too.
#reason test/providers-table.test.ts Pins the remote aliases of each provider.
#story A pull request merged by squash shows as merged
#step actor Reviewer
#step action opens the Lantern tab of a GitHub project
#file src/main/lantern-host-status.ts
#file src/main/lantern-host-github.ts
#step subject a pull request merged with Squash and merge
#file test/lantern-host-github.test.ts
#below interaction sees it merged, not open
#file test/e2e/pr-host-state.spec.ts
#below consequence shown as open => shown as merged
#story The host decides, and a failure keeps the git state
#step actor Reviewer
#step action refreshes with no account or a failing request
#file src/main/lantern-host-drivers.ts
#step subject the state of each pull request
#below interaction keeps the git state and reads one note
